{"name":"Eucalyptus Wreath","hex":"#88927e","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"eucalyptus","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of many trees, of genus Eucalyptus, native mainly to Australia.","Any tree of the tribe Eucalypteae, especially of the genera Corymbia and Angophora formerly classified in the Eucalyptus genus."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/eucalyptus"},{"term":"wreath","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Something twisted, intertwined, or curled.","An ornamental circular band made, for example, of plaited flowers and leaves, and used as decoration; a garland or chaplet, especially one given to a victor."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Alternative spelling of wreathe."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wreath"}],"entries":[{"title":"Eucalyptus","blocks":[{"text":"Eucalyptus is a genus of more than 700 species of flowering plants in the family Myrtaceae. Most species of Eucalyptus are trees, often mallees, and a few are shrubs. Along with several other genera in the tribe Eucalypteae, including Corymbia and Angophora, they are commonly known as eucalypts or \"gum trees\". Species of Eucalyptus have bark that is either smooth, fibrous, hard, or stringy and leaves that have oil glands. The sepals and petals are fused to form a \"cap\" or operculum over the stamens, hence the name from Greek eû 'well' and kaluptós 'covered'."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Eucalyptus_tereticornis_flowers%2C_capsules%2C_buds_and_foliage.jpeg/330px-Eucalyptus_tereticornis_flowers%2C_capsules%2C_buds_and_foliage.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eucalyptus"},{"title":"Wreath","blocks":[{"text":"A wreath is an assortment of flowers, leaves, fruits, twigs, or various materials that is constructed to form a ring shape."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/Ch